# Use RubyLLM for AI

Do not install `ruby_llm` until AI work is requested. When it is, that gem is the only LLM client.

RubyLLM already covers chat, tools (`RubyLLM::Tool`), agents, streaming, embeddings, images, transcription, structured output, and Rails persistence (`acts_as_chat`). Do not wrap Faraday, Net::HTTP, or a provider SDK around OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or similar for those jobs.

```ruby
# bad
gem "ruby-openai"
response = Faraday.post("https://api.openai.com/v1/chat/completions", ...)
```

```ruby
# good
gem "ruby_llm"
chat = RubyLLM.chat
chat.with_tools(LookupCustomer)
chat.ask("Why did Acme's bill double?")
```

Do not add `ruby-openai`, `openai`, `anthropic`, or `langchainrb` next to it.
